# SDCC and assembler outputs
*.rel
*.ihx
*.asm
*.lst
*.map
*.sym
*.noi
*.cdb

# ...but lib/server_crt0.asm is the ONE *.asm the build never writes: it is
# the hand-written userspace server startup that FS/MM/PM link, and the same
# glob that keeps build output out of the index kept the source out with it.
# That is why `make clean` deleting it was not recoverable from git, and why
# the build stopped at "No rule to make target lib/server_crt0.asm".  The
# exception mirrors the /test_host/ one above: name the source, keep the glob.
!lib/server_crt0.asm

# *.lk is NOT here, and used to be.  These are hand-written linker scripts, not
# toolchain output: sdldz80 takes one with -f and never writes one.  Measured by
# cleaning and rebuilding and comparing the set of .lk files before and after -
# identical, seven files, all of them inputs.  Each app's link rule names one as
# a prerequisite (`apps/date.ihx: apps/date.rel apps/date.lk ...`), so an
# untracked script means no place to put the code and no way to link it.
# tools/check_link_scripts.rb fails the build if one goes missing or untracked.

# Local root-level test binaries and host build products
/test_*
# ...but not the host harness source.  `/test_*` is meant for the root-level
# test binaries a Z80 test build leaves behind; it also matches test_host/,
# which is source, and an untracked z80_io_host.c means z80_outb is undefined
# and every host test that reaches the bank model silently reports as not
# linkable.  Measured by checking the file in.
!/test_host/
/build/
/platform/zeta-v2/test_kernel/test_bank_model
*.o
*.a

# Editor and OS metadata
.DS_Store
.vscode/
*.d

# Generated build identity, printed in the shell banner
shell/muzix_build_stamp.h
